{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/146656-one-world-or-many","id":146656,"title":"One world or many?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-23T06:39:44-07:00","id":146656,"title":"One world or many?","content":"Do you see Cwod as many worlds or one?<br /> <br /> its a lot less Pluralistic then NWod is why I ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:19:40-07:00","id":146697,"title":"","content":"I see it as many worlds. There are many aspects to the various game lines that are mutually exclusive or at least highly unlikely to coexist. Furthermore, the themes of the various lines are so different that they cannot be combined without damaging at least one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:45:09-07:00","id":146729,"title":"","content":"There was a talk with Justin Achille, Bill Bridges, and a couple other former long time White Wolf folks at DragonCon last year. This question came up, and I found their response fascinating.<br /> <br /> They were in unanimous agreement that the original intention for cWoD was a single shared world for all the game lines. Unfortunately, the realities of schedules and deadlines meant the folks working on one game line didn't always know what the folks working on the other games were doing, so contradictions between them came up. As time went on, different folks came up with different explanations for the contradictions. Eventually, they just decided to discourage crossover between the game lines. Although, every one of them said they still see the classic World of Darkness as one shared setting.<br /> <br /> My personal take is that the various game lines are different bubbles of reality all residing in the same world. From a distance, it all looks like one shared reality, but when you get inside those bubbles, the differences become apparent. Occasionally, those bubbles will collide and crossover is possible. It's like Buffy and Angel - two TV shows that nominally exist in the same world and will have an occasional crossover episode, but for the most part they're doing their own thing without too much concern for what the other one is doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:40:27-07:00","id":146803,"title":"","content":"My personal take is that this is one world with need for some trimming. In my case there were some drastic changes. I completely disregarded Mummy, Hunter, Kindred of the East, Demon and Changeling and replaced them with either my own concepts or what I deemed good from nWoD equivalents, compatible of course with the rest of cosmology. For the rest, I did some subtle changes just to make remaining gamelines as compatible as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T09:42:57-07:00","id":146858,"title":"","content":"I always figured that between Mage establishing that reality is flexible and Demon putting the cap on it by bringing up the &quot;multilayer&quot; reality, they were all existing together and that the inconsistencies were misinformation (intentional or accidental) and someone mucking around with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T10:26:14-07:00","id":146865,"title":"","content":"I've always seen it as one world, where the differences are mostly about misinformation and perspective. There are some contradictions between the lines but there are as many or more little things that confirm the one world theory, Tremere/OoH, Sluagh/Keremet/Wraith, Giovanni/Wraith, Silent Striders/Setites etc. And that is literally just scratching the surface. Every claim to separate the world into worlds has just felt wrong and forced to me but naturally YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T10:38:29-07:00","id":146871,"title":"","content":"PookaKnight and Papa Bear, those are the interpretations I use for OWoD. The &quot;Fractured Cosmos&quot; setting is how I believe the authors refer to it. When the Gauntlet rose, the Sundering occurred, the One left Creation with most of the angels -- something broke, the Cycle started in full swing, and the Tellurian started limping along through the ages. Like an unbalanced washing machine, once that little fracture happened, things just got worse... and worse... and worse. Until we get to the 6th Age, and the Weaver is insane, the Wyrm is even more insane, the Wyld was always insane, Nephandi are crawling out of the cracks in the heavens, Demons are crawling out of the cracks in hell, the dead are Rising, the Messengers are going &quot;F***! F***! The house is a mess and Dad's coming home!&quot;<br /> <br /> It <i>was</i> a single, unified world, but then something broke, and the layers of reality started slowly shifting like the laminated sheets in plywood becoming unglued from each other. It's still a single &quot;world&quot;, but there are different points of reference -- and each point of reference has very real, definable, and measurable differences. In an older and long-running Mage game of mine, the End Times had the various cosmologies <i>literally</i> crashing into each other. The various levels of reality were collapsing back into a single, unified world, as the foundations of reality were collapsing. It led to the various supernaturals encountering each other much more frequently than before, and forced a large majority of them to work together to make sure that the world didn't implode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T10:49:39-07:00","id":146877,"title":"","content":"Well, I don't really agree with lustral_star - I see them all as the same world wish some miscommunication going on - but that was a damn good explanation, and believable to boot. I could see using that as a basis for one of my games in the future (if it ever comes up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/426-big-brother","name":"Big Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar426_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T11:00:30-07:00","id":146884,"title":"","content":"Big Brother, that's the standard go-to for most WoD gamers I know. It makes sense, it's easy, and it can cause some interesting RP opportunities when the various entities encounter each other (&quot;You do <i>what</i>? Oh, wow, all this time I thought that vampirism was a <i>disease</i>!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, for the metaplot of my game, I had to dig a bit deeper and answer questions with more detail than just &quot;This group was right, this group was wrong&quot;. I wanted to cultivate a sense of something <i>big</i> happening in the world, and encourage the idea that the literal <i>fate of reality itself</i> is going to be hanging in the balance. I believe the official blurb for the &quot;Fractured Cosmos&quot; idea is toward the back in one of the later Mage sourcebooks... unfortunately, at the moment, I don't remember which one it's in. Probably Ascension, or one of the Storyteller Handbooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T11:07:30-07:00","id":146888,"title":"","content":"Not one, but many. So I don't ever have to visit or contemplate the existence of Postmodern Consensus Land.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T11:11:43-07:00","id":146892,"title":"","content":"One world with trimming; I generally just stick with Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Wraith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T12:25:55-07:00","id":147004,"title":"","content":"One world, different facets and perspectives. Things like the Garou believing in the Triat don't affect Kindred, because the vampires don't care what the filthy Lupines think; or, Mages' Consensual Reality\u2122 doesn't affect anyone else, because no one else believes in it but the Will-workers. Just like our world has myriad histories and beliefs, so to does the cWoD.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T03:50:46-07:00","id":147761,"title":"","content":"Many worlds.<br /> <br /> I feel that having a fruit salad of all the various supernaturals detracts from whatever we are playing.<br /> <br /> That said, we do use the simple Werewolves from the Vampire book, and the Triat as the universal 'truth', in our Vampire chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/919-harlokin","name":"harlokin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:33:04-07:00","id":148136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/146656-one-world-or-many?p=146858#post146858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always figured that between Mage establishing that reality is flexible and Demon putting the cap on it by bringing up the &quot;multilayer&quot; reality, they were all existing together and that the inconsistencies were misinformation (intentional or accidental) and someone mucking around with reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly this! <br /> I never understood why people hate dtf so much because it &quot;contradicts&quot; their favorite game-line's history/creation-myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:43:25-07:00","id":148145,"title":"","content":"A lot of people I've spoken to who hate D:tF claim it is because it &quot;declares&quot; the Judeo-Christian ideology to be the true interpretation of reality, and makes most of the other game lines cosmologies moot.<br /> <br /> Except, you know, the Demons have all gone <i>balls-to-the-wall crazy</i> while in the Abyss. It was implied in some of the books (and outright stated by some authors out of the books) that the Demons only had access to <i>parts</i> of reality -- they were seeing one tiny section of Creation, and then saying &quot;Yep! This is what Creation looks like! There can in no way be a part of Creation in which I did not take direct participation of its creation at the Beginning!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T15:28:32-07:00","id":148193,"title":"","content":"I consider each game to be it's own world. They may share some elements but they're still different. So a VtM game does not need to porteay the Lupines as Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3117-lucius","name":"Lucius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T00:13:22-07:00","id":148450,"title":"","content":"I always thought they were one world seen through many different views. each splat giving its explanation for its world view in their own book. personally at least i thought that garou were always more interesting than lupines as there never seemed to be any explanation for why they hate vampires in masquerade beyond &quot;because that's what werewolves do.&quot; and the attitude was always &quot;if you want to know more, check out werewolf: the apocalypse.&quot; in the end each group always does what they like anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T08:10:13-07:00","id":150356,"title":"","content":"I found Wraith worked with every game, but otherwise I saw the games as being self-contained. If I was running Mage, there were Kindred, a Camarilla, etc, but they weren't &quot;right&quot; about their past, and the ancient Vampires weren't in control of the world the way they were in Vampire. In a Vampire game, there was no Technocracy or Awakened Mages, but Sorcerer was handy. I would combine Werewolf and Mage often (they didn't contradict each other much).<br /> <br /> I also liked to say that, in the book you're running, the cosmology of the game was true for all other games while you were running the game. I'm running Werewolf? Vampires are a consistent formori strain. They might not know it, but they are. Mages are Gaia Formori of a kind. I'm running Vampire? Modern Mages practice Thaumaturgy and Necromancy. Werewolves are Lupines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3078-coffee-zombie","name":"Coffee Zombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T10:16:51-07:00","id":150480,"title":"","content":"I prefer the one-world interpretation, with pretty much every human and supernatural very ignorant or misinformed about a lot of things outside their immediate experience.<br /> <br /> I like Werewolf best and know only a little about most other gamelines, so I see the overall cosmology as more Werewolf-slanted in the places of contraditions. But I like to view each splat's origin story as true as possible, and try to see how they can exist together. I see a few &quot;consensual&quot; traits but mostly only in the Umbra, not the physical world. So for example, to the shapeshifters the Triat is three intelligent, self-aware mega-spirits with minds and desires and servants, while to the Traditions the Metaphysic Trinity is three flavors of impersonal essence that color and influence supernatural entitites. Both are right, but the three forces do exist and are metaphysically very important in the cosmos.<br /> <br /> One of the ways this works for me is that when a splat claims that their God or Goddess or whoever created them and the world and everything in it, I accept that said deity created that splat, but isn't necessarily the top of the heap and doesn't resemble their interpretation of it. There is a major god who cursed the Cainites, and a major earth goddess who created the werewolves, and an august personage of jade who cursed the Wan Xian, and a major god against whom the Demons rebelled... but none is THE Supreme Being who created or rules the whole universe.<br /> <br /> I also tend to throw Exalted in as the prehistory, because I always liked that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T11:53:20-07:00","id":151550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gaia Formori </div> </div> </div>People (more commonly animals, plants and objects) permamently possessed by Gaian spirits are Kami. Consistently on the side of Gaia, though Changing Breeds view them with some suspicion or so I heard (because Gaia, despite having shifters, creates beings who are not shifters yet too are her agents. Think of rivalry between governmental agencies).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T16:08:55-07:00","id":151792,"title":"","content":"Setting wise i consider them one world. However i dont have any interest in Demon, kue jin, changeling, wraith or mummy. So maybe the issues from most comes from them<br /> <br /> However mechanic wise they are kinda imcompatible. V20 and W20 have some differences in their systems and Mage revised have the propper rules for multi action. And Werewolf are so powerful that i have run into problems making a supernatural avengers game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T18:34:28-07:00","id":151904,"title":"","content":"I run them as one world, though being pre-6th Maelstrom - so no Demon or Orpheus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1082-nfi","name":"NFI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T05:03:15-07:00","id":152365,"title":"","content":"I've done prettymuch what Katsura and others have done. One world with some editing and adjustments. I try and stick with the 5 original main game lines, but I'm not against allowing in a Hunter or Demon player into my game as long as they are aware the perspective of the game is going to be heavily influenced by the other systems. I try and stick with one system and let it touch on the other 4. I blame having played online in White-Wolf's original chats for this perspective. I feel old for admitting I remember when there were only about 7 or 8 rooms. Two Vampire rooms, one for each of the other four systems, Shadow's Bar for everything and the OOC room. There was really no avoiding that the 5 systems all existed in one world and it made for some pretty crazy games. As soon as there were more rooms to expand into then every system seemed more isolated and more its own universe that didn't have to acknowledge any other world's circumstances. This still made for good games, but it's definitely a different feeling. More like a clique. It has its merits and flaws and I've carried the online gaming experience with me to my own TT games. It's given me an appreciation for unpredictable diversity to keep the game fresh. As long as the ST can keep the game systems working together, the players can enjoy it. When too many world's collide at once it can be a disaster. So it all comes down to what the ST can handle and where the dividing lines get drawn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T06:42:19-07:00","id":152456,"title":"","content":"I tend to run with 1-world interpretations. I've never found the differences in the settings especially fundamental, given how little the various factions understand about the things they do interact with (and due to how much White Wolf always put into emphasising that the underlying aspects of the world tended to warp to the observer's expectations). It requires tweaking a few things (the nature of Caine's Judge, a few terminological tweaks around the Umbra, re-emphasise just how unclear the Fallen's memories are), but very little that really impacts typical play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>---------------------------------------------<br /> Supporter of Spirits getting full playable splat design come Exalted 3E.<br /> Refugee from the 3rd Great Edition Wars of D&amp;D. <br /> oWoD Latecomer, Exalted Optimist, Scion ST, Trinity Curious","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/955-yue-ryong","name":"Yue Ryong","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar955_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"147"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T06:51:42-07:00","id":152461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/146656-one-world-or-many?p=146884#post146884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Big Brother, that's the standard go-to for most WoD gamers I know. It makes sense, it's easy, and it can cause some interesting RP opportunities when the various entities encounter each other (&quot;You do <i>what</i>? Oh, wow, all this time I thought that vampirism was a <i>disease</i>!&quot;)<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, for the metaplot of my game, I had to dig a bit deeper and answer questions with more detail than just &quot;This group was right, this group was wrong&quot;. I wanted to cultivate a sense of something <i>big</i> happening in the world, and encourage the idea that the literal <i>fate of reality itself</i> is going to be hanging in the balance. I believe the official blurb for the &quot;Fractured Cosmos&quot; idea is toward the back in one of the later Mage sourcebooks... unfortunately, at the moment, I don't remember which one it's in. Probably Ascension, or one of the Storyteller Handbooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was in the supplement that dealt with the <i>fate of reality itself</i>: <b>Ascension</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200bI also prefer the Many Worlds Interpretation, in part because it means that I don\u2019t have to be consistent from one chronicle to the next: when I\u2019m in a <b>Mage</b> game, mages warp reality through focused belief. When I\u2019m running <b>Werewolf</b>, their powers are spiritual in nature, and many are unwitting pawns of the Weaver (Technocrats, mostly), the Wyrm (Nephandi, mostly), or the Wyld (Marauders, mostly), up to and including having been empowered by something in the Triat. In a <b>Changeling</b> game, they\u2019re humans who have tapped into the power of the Dreaming. In a <b>Hunter</b> game, they\u2019re the Spellbound. In a <b>Demon</b> game, they\u2019re humans who have actualized their Faith Potential. And so on. It\u2019s like lustral_star\u2019s \u201cbubbles\u201d concept, with the added fact that the various bubbles are generally synchronized with each other: events tend to play out in mutually consistent ways for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T09:31:10-07:00","id":152602,"title":"","content":"Hey, there it is! Thank you kindly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T12:21:06-07:00","id":154087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/146656-one-world-or-many?p=147004#post147004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One world, different facets and perspectives. Things like the Garou believing in the Triat don't affect Kindred, because the vampires don't care what the filthy Lupines think; or, Mages' Consensual Reality\u2122 doesn't affect anyone else, because no one else believes in it but the Will-workers. Just like our world has myriad histories and beliefs, so to does the cWoD.<br /> <br /> Cheers!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much how I see it also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1441-ersatz","name":"Ersatz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-11T18:18:58-07:00","id":195161,"title":"","content":"My take on this is something like Katsura's (one world with small adjustments). From her list, I only discarded Mummy, Hunter and Demon, the other I could fit together.<br /> Instead of Hunter there were various types of people with different opinions why to fight &quot;monsters&quot;, like what is presented in V20 - Hunters Hunted II.<br /> Instead of Mummies the Dark Kingdom of Sand has just another kind of Wraiths, as the denizens of the Dark Kingdom of Jade also differ from the ones existing in the Dark Kingdom of Iron.<br /> Instead of Demon, there isn't anything, I don't like to mix that game, I like to play it apart from every other.<br /> However the other cWoD games (even Demon) could actually be fit into the Mage cosmology, it's the only tolerant one from the cWoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2554-sol","name":"Sol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}